# Multi-Step Wizard Pattern Standards

When a dialog has 3+ fields, complex workflows, or would benefit from guided user input, use the **wizard pattern** instead of a single-form approach. This pattern dramatically improves UX by reducing cognitive load.

## When to Use Wizards

| Use Wizard | Use Single Form |
|---|---|
| 3+ distinct information groups | 1-2 simple fields |
| Complex workflows with dependencies | Independent fields |
| User needs guidance/context | Self-explanatory inputs |
| Long forms that scroll | Fits on one screen |
| Data entry that benefits from focus | Quick edits |

**Examples requiring wizards:**
- Define Company Purpose (5 steps)
- Create Objective with Tasks (3+ steps)
- Onboarding flows
- Multi-part bookings
- Complex entity creation

**Examples NOT requiring wizards:**
- Edit title/description
- Simple confirmations
- Quick settings toggles

## The "Purpose Dialog Quality" Standard

The CompanyPurposeDialog (`src/components/objectives/company-purpose-dialog.tsx`) is the gold standard. All wizards should follow these principles:

### 1. Visual Progress Indicator

**REQUIRED**: All wizards must have a clear progress stepper with:
- Step icons (from lucide-react)
- Active/completed/pending visual states
- Connecting lines between steps

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Visual stepper with states
const STEPS = [
  { id: 'basic', title: 'Basic Info', icon: FileText },
  { id: 'details', title: 'Details', icon: Settings },
  { id: 'review', title: 'Review', icon: CheckCircle2 },
]

<div className="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
  {STEPS.map((step, index) => {
    const Icon = step.icon
    const isActive = step.id === currentStep
    const isCompleted = index < currentStepIndex

    return (
      <div key={step.id} className={cn('flex items-center gap-2 flex-1', index > 0 && 'pl-2')}>
        {/* Connector line */}
        {index > 0 && (
          <div className={cn(
            'h-0.5 flex-1',
            isCompleted ? 'bg-international-orange' : 'bg-muted'
          )} />
        )}
        {/* Step icon */}
        <div className={cn(
          'flex items-center justify-center rounded-full h-8 w-8 transition-colors',
          isActive && 'bg-international-orange text-white',
          isCompleted && !isActive && 'bg-orange-100 text-international-orange',
          !isActive && !isCompleted && 'bg-muted text-muted-foreground'
        )}>
          <Icon className="h-4 w-4" />
        </div>
      </div>
    )
  })}
</div>

// ❌ WRONG - No visual progress
<div>Step {currentStep} of {totalSteps}</div>

// ❌ WRONG - Text-only progress
<p>Step 2: Enter details</p>
```

### 2. Conversational Typography

**REQUIRED**: Each step must have:
- **Heading**: Clear question or action (`text-lg font-semibold`)
- **Description**: Context and guidance (`text-sm text-muted-foreground`)
- **Input label**: Field name with required indicator

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Conversational, guiding
<div className="space-y-4">
  <div>
    <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">
      Why does your company exist?
    </h3>
    <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Think beyond profit. What change do you want to make in the world? 
      What gets you out of bed every day?
    </p>
  </div>
  <div className="space-y-2">
    <Label htmlFor="whyExists">
      Your answer <span className="text-destructive" aria-label="required">*</span>
    </Label>
    <Textarea id="whyExists" placeholder="We exist to..." />
  </div>
</div>

// ❌ WRONG - Technical/cold
<div>
  <h3 className="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider">
    COMPANY PURPOSE
  </h3>
  <Label>Purpose Statement *</Label>
  <Textarea placeholder="Enter purpose" />
</div>

// ❌ WRONG - No guidance
<div>
  <Label>Purpose</Label>
  <Textarea />
</div>
```

### 3. One Focus Per Step

**REQUIRED**: Each step should ask about ONE concept or closely related group.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - One concept per step
// Step 1: Core Purpose
<StepCore question="Why does your company exist?" />

// Step 2: Problem & Audience (related concepts)
<StepAudience 
  problem="What problem are you solving?"
  audience="Who are you solving it for?"
/>

// Step 3: Differentiation  
<StepDifferentiation question="What makes you unique?" />

// ❌ WRONG - Multiple unrelated concepts
<div>
  <Input label="Purpose" />
  <Input label="Mission" />
  <Input label="Vision" />
  <Input label="Target Audience" />
  <Input label="Unique Value" />
  <Input label="5-Year Goals" />
</div>
```

### 4. Step Validation Before Proceeding

**REQUIRED**: Validate current step before allowing Next.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Validate before proceeding
const validateStep = (step: string): boolean => {
  switch (step) {
    case 'basic':
      if (!formData.title?.trim()) {
        setError('Please enter a title')
        return false
      }
      return true
    case 'details':
      if (!formData.description?.trim()) {
        setError('Please provide a description')
        return false
      }
      return true
    default:
      return true
  }
}

const goToNextStep = () => {
  if (!validateStep(currentStep)) return
  // ... proceed to next step
}

// ❌ WRONG - No validation
const goToNextStep = () => {
  setCurrentStep(nextStep) // User can skip required fields
}
```

### 5. Clear Navigation Flow

**REQUIRED**: Footer with Cancel/Back on left, Next/Submit on right.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Clear navigation
<DialogFooter>
  <div className="flex w-full items-center justify-between">
    <Button
      variant="secondary"
      onClick={isFirstStep ? onClose : goToPrevStep}
    >
      {isFirstStep ? 'Cancel' : (
        <>
          <ChevronLeft className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
          Back
        </>
      )}
    </Button>

    {isLastStep ? (
      <Button onClick={handleSubmit}>
        <CheckCircle2 className="h-4 w-4 mr-2" />
        Save
      </Button>
    ) : (
      <Button onClick={goToNextStep}>
        Next
        <ChevronRight className="h-4 w-4 ml-2" />
      </Button>
    )}
  </div>
</DialogFooter>

// ❌ WRONG - Confusing button placement
<DialogFooter>
  <Button onClick={goToNextStep}>Next</Button>
  <Button onClick={handleSubmit}>Save</Button>
  <Button onClick={onClose}>Cancel</Button>
</DialogFooter>
```

### 6. Character Limits with Counters

**REQUIRED**: For text fields, show character count and limit.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Character counter
const CHARACTER_LIMITS = {
  title: 200,
  description: 500,
}

<Textarea
  value={value}
  onChange={(e) => onChange(e.target.value)}
  maxLength={CHARACTER_LIMITS.description}
/>
<p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
  {value.length} / {CHARACTER_LIMITS.description} characters
</p>

// ❌ WRONG - No feedback on limits
<Textarea maxLength={500} />
```

### 7. Focus Management

**REQUIRED**: Auto-focus first input when step changes.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Focus management
const goToNextStep = () => {
  if (!validateStep(currentStep)) return
  setCurrentStep(nextStep)
  
  // Focus first input in next step
  setTimeout(() => {
    const firstInput = document.querySelector<HTMLInputElement | HTMLTextAreaElement>(
      'input:not([disabled]), textarea:not([disabled])'
    )
    firstInput?.focus()
  }, 100)
}

// ❌ WRONG - No focus management
const goToNextStep = () => {
  setCurrentStep(nextStep)
  // User must manually click into field
}
```

### 8. Error Display

**REQUIRED**: Show validation errors clearly using Alert.

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Clear error display
{error && (
  <Alert variant="destructive">
    <AlertCircle className="h-4 w-4" />
    <AlertDescription>{error}</AlertDescription>
  </Alert>
)}

// ❌ WRONG - Subtle/hidden errors
{error && <p className="text-red-500 text-xs">{error}</p>}
```

## Step Component Pattern

Extract each step into its own component for clarity:

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Extracted step components
function StepBasicInfo({
  title,
  description,
  onTitleChange,
  onDescriptionChange,
  titleLimit,
  descriptionLimit,
}: StepBasicInfoProps) {
  return (
    <div className="space-y-4">
      <div>
        <h3 className="text-lg font-semibold mb-2">
          What do you want to achieve?
        </h3>
        <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
          Give your objective a clear, actionable title that captures your goal.
        </p>
      </div>
      
      <div className="space-y-2">
        <Label htmlFor="title">
          Objective title <span className="text-destructive">*</span>
        </Label>
        <Input
          id="title"
          value={title}
          onChange={(e) => onTitleChange(e.target.value)}
          placeholder="e.g., Launch MVP by Q2"
          maxLength={titleLimit}
        />
        <p className="text-xs text-muted-foreground">
          {title.length} / {titleLimit} characters
        </p>
      </div>
      
      {/* Additional fields... */}
    </div>
  )
}

// ❌ WRONG - All steps inline in main component
function WizardDialog() {
  return (
    <Dialog>
      <DialogContent>
        {currentStep === 'basic' && (
          <div>
            {/* 50+ lines of inline JSX */}
          </div>
        )}
        {currentStep === 'details' && (
          <div>
            {/* 50+ more lines */}
          </div>
        )}
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  )
}
```

## Wizard State Management

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT - Clean state management
type FormStep = 'basic' | 'details' | 'review'

const STEPS: { id: FormStep; title: string; icon: React.ElementType }[] = [
  { id: 'basic', title: 'Basic Info', icon: FileText },
  { id: 'details', title: 'Details', icon: Settings },
  { id: 'review', title: 'Review', icon: CheckCircle2 },
]

const [currentStep, setCurrentStep] = useState<FormStep>('basic')
const [formData, setFormData] = useState<FormData>({...})
const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null)

const currentStepIndex = STEPS.findIndex(s => s.id === currentStep)
const isFirstStep = currentStepIndex === 0
const isLastStep = currentStepIndex === STEPS.length - 1
```

## Color Guidelines for Wizards

| Element | Token | Usage |
|---|---|---|
| Active step | `bg-international-orange text-white` | Current step indicator |
| Completed step | `bg-orange-100 text-international-orange` | Past steps |
| Pending step | `bg-muted text-muted-foreground` | Future steps |
| Connector (completed) | `bg-international-orange` | Line between completed steps |
| Connector (pending) | `bg-muted` | Line before current step |
| Primary CTA | `bg-international-orange` | Save/Submit button on final step |

## Quick Checklist

Before committing any wizard:

- [ ] Has visual progress stepper with icons
- [ ] Uses `international-orange` for active/completed states
- [ ] Each step has conversational heading + description
- [ ] One concept per step (or closely related group)
- [ ] Step validation before proceeding
- [ ] Clear Cancel/Back left, Next/Submit right
- [ ] Character counters on text fields
- [ ] Auto-focus first input on step change
- [ ] Errors displayed with Alert component
- [ ] Steps extracted into separate components
- [ ] Uses `size="lg"` on DialogContent
- [ ] Has `max-h-[90vh]` for tall content

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Solution |
|---|---|---|
| Single long form | Overwhelming, high cognitive load | Break into focused steps |
| Text-only progress | Users can't see where they are | Visual stepper with icons |
| Uppercase labels | Feels cold/technical | Conversational questions |
| No guidance text | Users don't understand context | Add helpful descriptions |
| Skip validation | Incomplete data submitted | Validate before Next |
| Inline step content | Hard to maintain, cluttered | Extract step components |
| Generic placeholders | No guidance on input format | Helpful, specific examples |

